T-Time
======

Third-party material and how it is used. Licence verification status is stated
honestly; "unverified" means not yet checked.

- pyewts 1.0.0 (Apache-2.0): the inventory of standard implicit stacks in
  `STANDARD_STACKS` (crates/ttime-core/src/ewts/mod.rs) was derived in part from
  its published list, cross-checked against m17n behaviour. Also used as a
  differential oracle (not shipped).
- ewts-rs / crate `ewts` 0.1.4 (MIT OR Apache-2.0): differential oracle
  (`scripts/differential/ewts-rs-diff`, not shipped); the 16 inputs and expected
  outputs in `crates/ttime-core/tests/fixtures/thl_rules.tsv` come from its
  `rules_test.rs`, which transcribes THL rule examples.
- Keyman `tibetan_ewts` keyboard (MIT): behavioural reference and differential
  testing only; no rules copied.
- m17n-db `bo-ewts.mim` (LGPL 2.1+): behavioural reference only; no tables or
  text copied. Stack inventory agreement was checked by behaviour, not by copying.
- Botok, Tibetan NLP, TiSpell, OpenPecha, BDRC: unverified; unused.

- Noto Serif Tibetan (SIL Open Font License 1.1): bundled in the macOS app
  (`macos/Resources/NotoSerifTibetan.ttf`, a format conversion of the web
  playground's copy, not subset or renamed) and in the web playground, for T-Time's
  own windows. Licence text: `macos/Resources/OFL-NotoSerifTibetan.txt`, also shown
  in the installer. The font may be redistributed with this software; it may not be
  sold on its own.

- Sanskrit (IAST) word list (`data/sanskrit/iast-lexicon.tsv`, bundled in the macOS app):
  headwords from Monier-Williams (1899) and Edgerton's Buddhist Hybrid Sanskrit
  Dictionary (1953) as digitised by the Cologne Digital Sanskrit Lexicon (Copyright 2014
  The Sanskrit Library and Thomas Malten, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0), with lemma counts from
  Hellwig's Digital Corpus of Sanskrit (CC BY 4.0). The list is distributed under
  CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, so non-commercial use only, and is not covered by the code licence;
  see `data/sanskrit/README.md` for the open questions about these terms.

T-Time's own code is licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0 (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE).
The illustrations and logos were made for T-Time and are not covered by that grant; see the README.
